# Changelog

## [Unreleased]

### Breaking Changes

- **Commands now use explicit namespaces.** Root action commands, plural `repos`, implicit
  skill-ID reads, and the hidden `mcp register` alias were removed. MCP tool names now include the
  complete command path. Migration table:

  | Removed path | Replacement |
  | --- | --- |
  | `init` | `project init` |
  | `install` | `project install` |
  | `add`, `remove`, `update`, `list`, `read`, `search` | `skill add`, `skill remove`, `skill update`, `skill list`, `skill read`, `skill search` |
  | `add BUNDLE.zip`, `list --bundles` | `bundle add BUNDLE.zip`, `bundle list` |
  | `update --bundle ID --from FILE`, `remove --bundle ID` | `bundle update ID --from FILE`, `bundle remove ID` |
  | `repos ACTION` | `repo ACTION` |
  | `analyze ACTION` | `analysis ACTION` |
  | `optimize ACTION` | `optimization ACTION` |
  | `reindex` | `index rebuild` |
  | `serve` | `server serve` |
  | `doctor`, `completion`, `spec` | `cli doctor`, `cli completion`, `cli spec` |
  | `mcp register` | `mcp install` |
  | `fastskill SKILL_ID` | `fastskill skill read SKILL_ID` |

  `bundle build`, `bundle override`, `marketplace`, `eval`, `cache`, and `mcp` retain their
  namespaces. See the [migration guide](webdocs/cli-reference/command-migration.mdx) for complete
  invocations and MCP tool-name replacements.

- **CLI command-surface redesign: four commands removed (issue #183).**
  `fastskill resolve`, `fastskill sync`, `fastskill disable`, and `fastskill show` have been
  removed with no hidden aliases. Migration table:

  | Removed command | Replacement |
  |---|---|
  | `fastskill resolve <query>` | `fastskill skill search <query> --local --paths --json` |
  | `fastskill show [id]` | `fastskill skill read <id> --meta` (by id) or `fastskill skill list` (all) |
  | `fastskill show <id> --tree` | `fastskill skill read <id> --tree` |
  | `fastskill sync` | No replacement — agents read the skills directory directly |
  | `fastskill disable <id>` | `fastskill skill remove <id>` |

  Shell completion scripts auto-derive from the registered command tree and no longer suggest
  the removed commands.

- **`fastskill index rebuild` exits 0 when no embedding provider is configured** (previously
  exited 1). If a CI pipeline relied on indexing failure to detect missing configuration, switch
  to `fastskill cli doctor` instead.

- **Skill and project lifecycle commands now auto-trigger `index rebuild`** after a successful
  run when an embedding provider is configured. Pass `--no-reindex` or set
  `auto_reindex = false` in `[tool.fastskill]` of `skill-project.toml` to opt out.

### Added

- **`fastskill cli doctor`**: new diagnostics command that reports environment readiness
  (skills directory, `skill-project.toml`, embedding provider, API key, auth token). Exits 0
  when no hard failures; exits 1 when the skills directory is inaccessible. `--json` flag emits
  a JSON array of `{check, status, message}` objects.

- **`fastskill skill read --meta` / `--tree`**: `skill read` now accepts `--meta` (structured metadata),
  `--tree` (dependency tree), `--locked`, `--format`, and `--json`. These flags replace
  `fastskill show` entirely.

- **`fastskill skill search --paths` / `--content`**: local search gains `--paths` (emit absolute
  SKILL.md path per result, forces JSON) and `--content <none|preview|full>` (include skill
  content). Both flags require `--local`.

- **`auto_reindex` config field**: `[tool.fastskill]` in `skill-project.toml` accepts
  `auto_reindex = false` to disable the new automatic reindex side-effect globally.

- **All internal API routes moved from `/api/<path>` to `/api/v1/<path>`.**
  Affected endpoints include `/api/skills`, `/api/project`, `/api/status`, `/api/search`,
  `/api/resolve`, `/api/reindex`, `/api/registry/…`, and `/api/manifest/…`.
  Update any client URL strings from `/api/…` to `/api/v1/…`.
  Unversioned `/api/…` requests are redirected with HTTP 308 to the corresponding `/api/v1/…`
  path, providing a temporary migration bridge for existing clients.

### Added

- **Liveness probe** (`GET /healthz`): Returns HTTP 200 with JSON `{status, version}` where
  `version` is the fastskill crate version. Suitable for Kubernetes, ECS, and Docker health checks.
- **Readiness probe** (`GET /readyz`): Returns HTTP 200 when the server is ready to accept
  traffic. Returns HTTP 503 while graceful shutdown is in progress.
- **`X-API-Version: v1` response header**: Present on all `/api/v1/…` responses to identify
  the API version that served the request.
- **Graceful shutdown**: Sending SIGINT or SIGTERM causes the server to drain in-flight requests,
  flip `/readyz` to 503, stop the `ValidationWorker` cleanly, and exit with code 0.

### Fixed

- **ValidationWorker leak**: The background validation task now exits cleanly when the server
  shuts down. Previously, the task was leaked on SIGINT/SIGTERM.
- **axum 0.8 route parameter syntax**: All route literals updated from `:param`/`*rest` (axum
  0.7 syntax) to `{param}`/`{*rest}` (axum 0.8 syntax), fixing a latent panic on parameterised
  routes at server startup.
- **Compression scope**: gzip (`CompressionLayer`) is now applied only to versioned application
  routes (`/api/v1/…`) rather than globally, leaving health probes and host routes uncompressed.

### Preserved Contracts

- `GET /v1/skills` and all `/v1/skills/{skill_id}/…` (Claude-compatible API surface) — URL
  unchanged, served via `mount("/v1")`.
- `GET /index/{*skill_id}` (raw skill index) — URL unchanged, served via `mount("/index")`.
- Console UI static files (`/`, `/index.html`, `/app.js`, `/styles.css`, `/dashboard`) —
  URLs unchanged.
- `fastskill server serve --host … --port …` CLI arguments — flags preserved under the new path.

### Dependencies

- `tower-http` bumped from `0.5` to `0.6` (required for `CorsLayer` type compatibility with
  cli-framework).
- `cli-framework` added as a git dependency (`features = ["api-server"]`) providing the
  versioned API server host.
- `tokio-util` `"sync"` feature added for `CancellationToken` support.
